-money-half-even-rounding", "confidence": 0.88}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 is open. Next I'll try the merge. Policy says it needs code-owner approval, so the merge should be sent to an approver automatically.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CVGTgyQ1S6viW73WdwkRPA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "confidence": 0.75}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and merged the fix into main, so it should ship in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding, but it actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I made a one-line change to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead.\n- **CI:** The test run (ci-0001) passed.\n- **PR:** I opened PR #101 against main without naming any reviewers. Merging needed a code owner's approval, which they gave (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), and the PR is merged.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID. The fix just follows what the code comment and the test expect.", "type": "text"}]}]}